      "side": 1,
      "message": "Am I right that this note does not cover a flap after the mountpoint is registered? Then setDeviceStatusReady() at DeviceConnectionManager.java throws synchronously, the connect future fails, GnmiNodeListener merges FAILURE plus failure-details, and the mountpoint stays up. The later READY from this branch only merges node-status, so failure-details stays forever. Suggest treating GnmiConnectionStatusException there as non-fatal once mounted, and/or deleting failure-details on the READY write.",
